{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Replaced and Nonreplaced Elements.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Replaced and Nonreplaced Elements.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"replaced and nonreplaced elements replaced and nonreplaced elements","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Replaced and Nonreplaced Elements.md","fileName":"Replaced and Nonreplaced Elements.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Replaced and Nonreplaced Elements","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 01:58\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[CSS Stylesheet Integration]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["CSS Stylesheet Integration","CSS Box Model","css_thedefinitiveguide.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Replaced and Nonreplaced Elements.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Replaced and Nonreplaced Elements.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"replaced and nonreplaced elements replaced and nonreplaced elements","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Replaced and Nonreplaced Elements.md","fileName":"Replaced and Nonreplaced Elements.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Replaced and Nonreplaced Elements","heading":"Replaced and Nonreplaced Elements","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A replaced element is rendered using content outside the document itself, such as an image supplied through a URL or a form control drawn by the user agent. CSS generally treats that external object as a unit with intrinsic dimensions instead of laying out its internal contents.\n\nA nonreplaced element has content represented within the document tree, so CSS constructs and formats boxes for that content directly. The distinction affects sizing, baselines, and inline formatting in the [[CSS Box Model]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["CSS Stylesheet Integration","CSS Box Model","css_thedefinitiveguide.pdf"],"properties":[],"page